{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat prompt.txt; echo '--- task.json'; cat task.json\"","aggregated_output":"After performing differential gene expression analysis comparing CBD/cisplatin treatment vs DMSO control (using padj < 0.05 and |log2FC| ≥ 0.5), followed by enrichment analysis using gseapy with Reactome_2022 gene sets, what is the overlap ratio (DEGs found in pathway / total pathway genes) for the 'TP53 Regulates Transcription Of Cell Cycle Genes' pathway in the enrichment results? Express your answer as a fraction (e.g., X/Y).\n\nUse only the files provided in this workspace.\nSolve the task using any local code, scripts, packages, shell commands, or public documentation you need. Galaxy is not required.\n\nInputs:\n- inputs/counts_raw_unfiltered.csv (6080359 bytes)\n- inputs/ensg_to_gene_name.tsv (2360408 bytes)\n- inputs/sample_layout.csv (2891 bytes)\n\nRun condition constraints:\n\n- You may use local shell commands, Python scripts, package installation,\n  internet access, and any code you write yourself to solve the task.\n- Use only files provided inside `/workspace` as benchmark inputs.\n- Do not inspect files outside `/workspace`.\n- Do not attempt to access hidden benchmark source rows, expected answers,\n  verifier files, or private metadata.\n- Keep the answer faithful to the question semantics; do not simplify the\n  task into a different question.\n\nScientific interpretation:\n\nUse appropriate scientific and domain knowledge to determine the requested\nestimand, analysis unit, data scope, preprocessing, method, and output semantics\nbefore choosing tools or running code. Interpret relevant supplied inputs and\nprovenance together. Do not let file layout, software defaults, tool\navailability, or execution convenience silently redefine the requested\nanalysis. When plausible interpretations materially change the result, choose\nthe interpretation best supported by the task and data before accepting the\nanswer.\n\nOutput:\n\n- The experiment runner records raw model events, usage, and exit status. Do\n  not create separate evidence, verification, or audit files.\n- Write `codex_output/answer.txt` before the final chat response only after the\n  requested quantity has been computed successfully.\n- `codex_output/answer.txt` — exactly one line, canonical answer only. No\n  labels, prose, Markdown, alternatives, citations, units labels, or caveats.\n  - Numbers: decimal or scientific notation, no thousands separators.\n  - Percentages: value + `%` only when the question asks for a percentage.\n  - Strings/genes/chromosomes: exact label only.\n  - Direction/category/choice answers: exact requested label only.\n\nA failed command or package is not evidence that the benchmark item has no\nsolution. Continue with a valid repair or alternate execution route within the\nactive runtime limits. If execution still fails, do not guess and do not write\n`answer.txt`.\n--- task.json\n{\n  \"tag\": \"bixbench\",\n  \"version\": \"1.5\",\n  \"question\": \"After performing differential gene expression analysis comparing CBD/cisplatin treatment vs DMSO control (using padj < 0.05 and |log2FC| \\u2265 0.5), followed by enrichment analysis using gseapy with Reactome_2022 gene sets, what is the overlap ratio (DEGs found in pathway / total pathway genes) for the 'TP53 Regulates Transcription Of Cell Cycle Genes' pathway in the enrichment results? Express your answer as a fraction (e.g., X/Y).\",\n  \"categories\": \"RNA-seq,Differential Expression Analysis,Transcriptomics\",\n  \"source\": \"BixBench-Verified-50\",\n  \"ground_truth_visible\": false\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
